These are selected adaptations to our own planning/Atlas product, not a whole-skill or runtime rebase. The touched prompt notices name this reviewed pin; untouched material keeps its earlier provenance. Local patches: bind both Momus and Oracle diagnostics to explicit dispatch-time path/round/kind and SHA-256, never infer a plan path from prompt prose; observe native final task outcomes without a new tool_result hook; contain storage in the planner's local artifacts, allocate exclusive numbered files, deduplicate reviewer sessions, fail open, and copy diagnostic history into the approved bundle without granting approval or row-completion authority. Keep the configurable reviewRoundLimit alongside prompt-level stagnation and owner-controlled continuation. Enforce new D-row origin dependencies in ledger v11 with an explicit blocksOrigin exception; v10 and earlier D rows retain their historical ordering and proof on load. Keep native isolation and owned-only cleanup, retaining resources required by unfinished PR delivery. Existing proportionality, LIGHT/HEAVY, unfinished blocked rows, native approval, and receipt contracts remain unchanged.
The native proposal marker is version 5 to carry optional diagnostic history through a fresh-session approval; version 3 and 4 markers remain accepted without that history, and neither marker provenance nor Atlas approval depends on review artifacts.

